GAL16V8
THORU4

A0   FC0  A16  A17  A18  A19  DS   PSEL RAM  GND
A15  BLK1 BLK0 EN   RA7  CAS1 CAS0 RAS0 RAS1 VCC

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Pin 7 (DS) is the bus /DS already inverted by U2: HIGH = data strobe active.
; PSEL = /Q of U3A: HIGH idle (row address on the 74LS257), LOW = column.
; RAM  =  Q of U3B: goes HIGH one half clock after PSEL goes LOW.
;
; Memory map (68008, 20 bit):
;   $00000-$3FFFF  QL motherboard (not ours)
;   $40000-$7FFFF  DRAM bank 0  U19,U21..U33  (pin 18 = /RAS, pin 17 = /CAS)
;   $80000-$BFFFF  DRAM bank 1  U18,U20..U32  (pin 19 = /RAS, pin 16 = /CAS)
;   $C0000-$FFFFF  BLK0: ROM board (74LS139 U5A -> NS1..NS3, NS0 free/slot)
;   $F8000-$FFFFF  data accesses (FC0=1) -> BLK1: I/O (A8-A14 not decoded)
;                  program fetches (FC0=0) stay in BLK0 (8K EPROM, NS3+A15)
;
; NOTE: the schematic net names of pins 16 and 19 are swapped (RAS2BK1 goes
; to the /CAS pins, CAS2BK1 to the /RAS pins). The pin names used here
; follow the real connection.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/BLK1 = DS * A19 * A18 * A17 * A16 * A15 * FC0

/BLK0 = DS * A19 * A18 * /A17
      + DS * A19 * A18 * /A16
      + DS * A19 * A18 * /A15
      + DS * A19 * A18 * /FC0

; The board takes the cycle (QL DSMC high via Q1, U1 enabled, DTACK)
EN = A19
   + A18

; Row (PSEL=1): A17, column (PSEL=0): A0
RA7 = PSEL * A17
    + /PSEL * A0

; Normal access: /RAS with DS, /CAS with RAM.
; CAS-before-RAS refresh of the bank that is NOT accessed, in every cycle
; outside $C0000-$FFFFF (QL board cycles and cycles to the other bank).
/RAS0 = DS * /A19 * A18
      + RAM * /A18
/CAS0 = RAM * /A19 * A18
      + DS * /A18

/RAS1 = DS * A19 * /A18
      + RAM * /A19
/CAS1 = RAM * A19 * /A18
      + DS * /A19

DESCRIPTION
CST Thor 20 expansion board, U4: memory decoder, DRAM RAS/CAS and refresh.
Reconstructed from the schematic and the Thor system ROM 5.22 (see
GAL_U4_U13.md). Not the original fuse map.
